  "holistic_F_H": -3,
  "section_notes": "S1 is fully safe with 24-hour reporting and suspected-incident coverage. S2 is weakened because there is no permanent numeric failure-rate cap; the 5% threshold only triggers review and regulator-authorized market retention. S3 and S4 are acceptable (6-year retrofit, 36-month built-in suppression), while S5 is acceptable because recall is mandatory at 8/100k but notices are only 'promptly' and no serious-injury clause is included."
